# SmartAsset Analytics project

Device stock and lifecycle tracking (check-in → transfer → check-out → install → repair → retire), multi-tenant.
Details: `docs/architecture.md`. User guide: `docs/user-guide/README.md`.

- `backend/` FastAPI + SQLAlchemy async + PostgreSQL/PostGIS with Row-Level Security
- `frontend/` Angular 22 + Syncfusion 32 Material 3 + Tailwind v4
- Deploy: `docker-compose.yml` (nginx, frontend, api, db); dev DB on `127.0.0.1:5434` via `docker-compose.dev.yml`

## Invariants

- User-facing text (UI labels, API error messages) is Thai. Code, comments and commit messages are English.
- The device state machine exists twice and must stay in sync:
  `backend/app/domain/rules.py` (`ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS`) and `frontend/src/app/core/device-actions.ts`.
- Enums (status, transaction type, role, repair order, document owner, audit entity) exist in
  `backend/app/domain/enums.py`, a CHECK constraint in migrations, `frontend/src/app/core/models.ts`
  and Thai labels in `frontend/src/app/core/labels.ts`.
- Every status change writes one `inventory_transactions` row in the same DB transaction.
  `SEND_REPAIR` / `QC_FAIL` also open (or refresh) a `repair_orders` row; `REPAIR_DONE` closes it.
- Never bypass tenant isolation: the app DB role is subject to RLS; do not query with the owner role outside migrations/tests.
  Moving a customer's `tenant_id` is superadmin-only and blocked while they have an active installation.

## Verification before commit

- Backend: `cd backend && uv run pytest` (API flow tests need the dev DB migrated + seeded)
- Frontend: `cd frontend && npx ng build`
- Commit per feature with a descriptive message (`feat:`, `fix(ui):`, `style:`, `docs:`).
